        <key>bodyEndSelection</key>
        <string>First lowest-body arrival after the native lower terminal cut, before its defining terminal chain.</string>
        <key>boundary</key>
        <string>New source hypothesis. A bounded control-point field is not a C1 curve or raster guarantee. Inspect rounded joins, actual native terminal identity, weight, spacing and compiled mark/feature/target-size behaviour separately.</string>
        <key>bounds</key>
        <array>
          <real>-3.0</real>
          <real>-216.0</real>
          <integer>477</integer>
          <integer>574</integer>
        </array>
        <key>construction</key>
        <string>Replace only the genuine SC S lower-left terminal curve/cut by the full purpose-coded native terminal chain. All three connection points are exact; independent vertical fitting keeps baseline-level first controls horizontal. Local bounded horizontal fitting avoids extrapolated stem deformation. No whole-capital scaling, ordinary S alias, clipped fragment pasted under a retained foot or external outline.</string>
        <key>correction</key>
        <string>The earlier full affine extrapolation produced an outer-stem detour in hooked BoldItalic, even after changing its deep translation anchor. Bound x displacement to the actual connection triangle. Use the outer cut to align the deep hook; use the bottom-bowl connection for the flowing swash. Preserve every other SC S body segment and every deep native terminal control through translation.</string>
        <key>deepTerminalTranslationX</key>
